  "construction_notes": [
    {
      "text": "Parcel match: source APN 022-38-007 was subdivided and isn't in county data. County situs 1353 and 1357 California Circle bracket 1355. Two lots stand in for the 6.69-acre site.",
      "src": [
        "SRC-001887"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "The 75 apartments in this count may be SCC-000575 (1397 California Circle, 75 units). Not merged: no source opened links them.",
      "src": [
        "SRC-001887"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "State report 2025 names two for-sale collections on the site: Apex at the District (townhomes) and Rise at the District (2-4 unit buildings).",
      "src": [
        "SRC-001128"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Pulte presentation posted by the city: site is 6.69 acres in the Dixon Landing Business Park (circa 1986) with 90,500 sq ft of existing industrial space; 36% affordable units; schedule shown as application April 2022, groundbreaking early 2024, opening late 2024/early 2025.",
      "src": [
        "SRC-002603"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "City Council approved unanimously (Nov 2023), removing the General Plan's 100% affordable requirement for the site; council allowed market-rate homes to be occupied before construction of the affordable apartments.",
      "src": [
        "SRC-002601"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "CTCAC staff report (Dec 10, 2025), CA Circle Family, 1355 California Circle, 0.94-acre site: 75 units (30 one-bedroom, 21 two-bedroom, 24 three-bedroom), developer Waterford Development, total cost $47,636,880; $1,815,835 annual federal credits and $12,486,492 tax-exempt bonds; Pulte Home Company contributes $6,400,000; construction expected June 2026 to January 2028; legal description and APN not yet finalized as part of a larger site.",
      "src": [
        "SRC-002602"
      ]
    }
  ],
